        <mxCell id="c238" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined in teal: the three threshold cells, links to the named cells of the Materiality sheet (each formula beside it). In blue: each pattern&#x27;s exposure for fiscal 2026, a link to the Tests sheet (the formula bar shows H8&#x27;s), and the combined groups&#x27; exposure and potential magnitude; the groups count each document once (D1, D2: 197,278.32, not the 240,822.22 the two patterns add up to). In coral: the band, a formula that reads the exposure against the three thresholds. In amber: the classification. In teal, the counts that follow it. The sheet goes on to row 44 with the clean results and the model answer. Hidden columns differ by block, long texts are cut.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="852" width="860" height="83" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
